data: {"research_task_id": "d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd", "event_seq": 6, "type": "worker", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T16:41:32Z", "payload": {"content_hash": "fca92358a25a3418b48b418da3d16a5a170136fefcafc47495b432a98cd19093", "node_key": "tool:d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd:s1:search_paper_catalog:04a04002e1c5", "node_type": "tool", "parent_node_key": "agent:d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd:s1", "parent_source_event_id": "research-event:d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd:3", "result_id": "search_paper_catalog", "result_length": 11166, "status": "completed", "summary": "检索完成：来源=USENIX Security（全局目录），命中 5 篇候选论文。\n1. Web Cache Deception Escalates!\n   catalog_paper_id: 240837c172070c94fb76db82dc400a9c\n   candidate: {\"title\":\"Web Cache Deception Escalates!\",\"catalog_paper_id\":\"240837c172070c94fb76db82dc400a9c\",\"conference_id\":\"usenix-security\",\"year\":2022,\"source_page_url\":\"[已隐藏链接]\",\"source_links\":[\"[已隐藏链接]\"]}\n   详情页: [已隐藏链接]\n   摘要: Web Cache Deception (WCD) tricks a web cache into erroneously storing sensitive content, thereby making it widely accessible on the Internet. In a USENIX Security 2020 paper titled \"Cached and Confused: Web Cache Deception in the Wild\", researchers presented the first systematic exploration of the attack over 340 websites. This state-of-the-art approach for WCD detection injects markers into websites and checks for leaks into caches. However, this scheme has two fundamental limitations: 1) It cannot probe websites that do not present avenues for marker injection or reflection. 2) Marker setup is a burdensome process, making lar", "tool_name": "search_paper_catalog"}}

