data: {"research_task_id": "d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd", "event_seq": 19, "type": "worker", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T16:41:32Z", "payload": {"content_hash": "fca92358a25a3418b48b418da3d16a5a170136fefcafc47495b432a98cd19093", "node_key": "tool:d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd:s3:search_paper_catalog:666283d214d9", "node_type": "tool", "parent_node_key": "agent:d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd:s3", "parent_source_event_id": "research-event:d5a3c7f89f2d5449b9bd3f59a2f67bfd:16", "result_id": "search_paper_catalog", "result_length": 10475, "status": "completed", "summary": "检索完成：来源=USENIX Security（全局目录），命中 5 篇候选论文。\n1. In-Kernel Control-Flow Integrity on Commodity OSes using ARM Pointer Authentication\n   catalog_paper_id: 179cb9c78ac1f2cb590a40d29e3a3350\n   candidate: {\"title\":\"In-Kernel Control-Flow Integrity on Commodity OSes using ARM Pointer Authentication\",\"catalog_paper_id\":\"179cb9c78ac1f2cb590a40d29e3a3350\",\"conference_id\":\"usenix-security\",\"year\":2022,\"source_page_url\":\"[已隐藏链接]\",\"source_links\":[\"[已隐藏链接]\"]}\n   详情页: [已隐藏链接]\n   摘要: This paper presents an in-kernel, hardware-based control-flow integrity (CFI) protection, called PAL, that utilizes ARM's Pointer Authentication (PA). It provides three important benefits over commercial, state-of-the-art PA-based CFIs like iOS's: 1) enhancing CFI precision via automated refinement techniques, 2) addressing hindsight problems of PA for inkernel uses such as preemptive hijacking and brute-forcing attacks, and 3) assuring the algorithmic or implementation correctness via post validation. PAL achieves these go", "tool_name": "search_paper_catalog"}}

